edia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Aerial_photo_of_Hoonah%2C_Alaska.jpg/960px-Aerial_photo_of_Hoonah%2C_Alaska.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Icy Strait Point is a cruise destination located in Hoonah, Alaska, established in 1996 by the Alaskan Native Huna Totem Corporation. The only privately owned cruise destination in Alaska, it is located on Chichagof Island and named after the nearby Icy Strait. Huna Totem Corporation is owned by approximately 1,350 Alaskan Natives with aboriginal ties to Hoonah and the Glacier Bay area.","wpu":"Icy Strait Point","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Cruise_ship_passengers_arrive_at_Icy_Strait_Point_2009.jpg/960px-Cruise_ship_passengers_arrive_at_Icy_Strait_Point_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}